## Proof

Let
$$S \;=\; \sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(2n+1)^{3}} \;=\; \sum_{\substack{k\ge 1\\ k\text{ odd}}}\frac{1}{k^{3}}.$$

Recall the Riemann zeta value
$$\zeta(3)\;=\;\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{k^{3}},$$
which is the sum over **all** positive integers. Split this sum into odd and even indices:
$$\zeta(3)\;=\;\sum_{\substack{k\ge 1\\k\text{ odd}}}\frac{1}{k^{3}}\;+\;\sum_{\substack{k\ge 1\\k\text{ even}}}\frac{1}{k^{3}}\;=\;S\;+\;\sum_{m=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(2m)^{3}}.$$

Factor the even-index sum:
$$\sum_{m=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(2m)^{3}}\;=\;\frac{1}{8}\sum_{m=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{m^{3}}\;=\;\frac{1}{8}\,\zeta(3).$$

Substituting back:
$$\zeta(3)\;=\;S\;+\;\tfrac{1}{8}\zeta(3).$$

Solving for $S$:
$$S\;=\;\zeta(3)-\tfrac{1}{8}\zeta(3)\;=\;\tfrac{7}{8}\,\zeta(3).$$

Therefore
$$\boxed{\displaystyle\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(2n+1)^{3}}\;=\;\frac{7}{8}\,\zeta(3)}.$$

